  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Logo Sets the Room",
    "overview": "Fortabella's supplied logo (cream blackletter with a gilded bevel, crimson wild roses with gold centres, olive leaves, a gold diamond between the two halves of the motto) is the one ornate object in every direction. Each direction builds a room around it: a blush boutique (Rosa y Oro), a black velvet jewellery box (Terciopelo), a tattoo flash sheet (Flash Sheet), a field of crimson petals (Flor Fuerte). The shop underneath is one system: same header, product card, filters, product page, quantity stepper, cart drawer and footer, written once in `shared/css/core.css` and `shared/js/store.js`, and fed by one data file, `shared/data/catalog.js`.\n\nThe project currently holds all four directions because the client has not chosen yet. A future build extends exactly one of them. Read the Shared sections first, then the block for the chosen direction, and ignore the other three. Never mix directions: the token names are shared, but each direction's values, shapes and buy colour belong to that direction alone.\n\nDensity is boutique, not marketplace: large display type, generous section padding (roughly 72px to 150px vertically), four-up product grids on desktop and two-up on phones. The primary visitor arrives from Instagram on a phone, so every interactive target is at least 44px tall.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One shared structural system (`core.css` + `store.js`) with four token sets, each in its direction's `theme.css`.",
      "The client logo is used exactly as supplied, never recoloured or redrawn.",
      "The motto always appears in both languages, joined by the logo's gold diamond.",
      "One filled colour means \"buy\" in each direction; every other button is outlined or ghosted.",
      "Sticker art and prices are labelled samples until the client supplies real ones.",
      "Fully bilingual: every UI string lives in EN and ES in `store.js`; sticker phrases stay in their original language."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Buy Colour Rule",
        "body": "Each direction has exactly one filled colour that means \"add to cart\": crimson in Rosa y Oro and Flash Sheet, gold in Terciopelo, rose in Flor Fuerte (gold only where the ground is itself rose). Secondary actions are outlined, ghosted or plain links. The \"added\" state swaps to a different fill (ink, olive or cream) so the buy colour never reads as a confirmation.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Field Rule",
        "body": "Each direction's home page carries one contrasting colour field and only one: wine in Rosa y Oro, cream in Terciopelo, black in Flash Sheet. Flor Fuerte is the exception by design: the rose field is its world (hero and collections), and its single contrasting band is the black statement.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase tracked labels above headings. The only caps in the system are inside the logo artwork itself.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real Material Rule",
        "body": "A material is either a real image or absent. Terciopelo's velvet is two generated photographic plates (`2-terciopelo/img/velvet-ground.webp` tiled at 512px behind the hero, `velvet-cushion.webp` behind every sticker, the charm, the product image, cart lines and collection art). Gradients, noise filters or shadows pretending to be velvet, paper, gold foil or tattoo ink are not used.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** set colours only through the shared token names in the chosen direction's `theme.css`; re-scope `--ink-soft`, `--sticker-edge` and `--focus` on any section that changes ground.",
      "**Do** keep exactly one filled buy colour per direction, and give the \"added\" state a different fill.",
      "**Do** use the logo lockup with its own tagline only on light grounds; use the mark plus live motto text everywhere else.",
      "**Do** show the motto in both languages, joined by the gold diamond.",
      "**Do** add every new sticker, pack or category as an entry in `shared/data/catalog.js`; set `image` when real art arrives and the stand-in art disappears.",
      "**Do** keep \"sample\" labelling on prices and sticker art (footer note and cart note) until the client supplies real values.",
      "**Do** honour `prefers-reduced-motion`: the shared rule cuts every animation and transition, and the Terciopelo sway and Flor rose rotation stop."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** recolour, redraw, crop the lettering of, or apply filters to the client logo.",
      "**Don't** fade or slide sections in one by one as they scroll into view; content is visible on load.",
      "**Don't** imitate materials (velvet, paper, foil, ink) with CSS gradients, noise or shadows; use a real image plate or nothing.",
      "**Don't** put small uppercase eyebrow labels above headings.",
      "**Don't** add a second filled button colour beside the buy colour in the same direction.",
      "**Don't** mix tokens, fonts or shapes from two directions in one build.",
      "**Don't** invent prices, reviews, testimonials or customer counts."
    ]
  }
}